 "scribe_vocals_2": {
  "text": "Erythrocyte, red blood cells. Most abundant of all the cell. Adult man on average has five to 5.5 millions of RBCs per cubic millimeter. Are these formed in the red bone marrow. Nucleus devoid in most mammals. Biconcave in shape. Hemoglobin, iron-containing complex protein. Red colored, hence the color, hence the name. Hemoglobin grams in every 100L, twelve to sixteen. Role, transport of respiratory gases. Lifespan, one hundred twenty days. Destroyed in the spleen, graveyard of RBCs. Hemoglobin, iron-containing complex protein. Red colored, hence the color, hence the name. Erythrocyte, red blood cells.",
